WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:09.092
A NETFLIX SERIES

00:45.086 --> 00:47.005
How much longer do we need to walk?

00:47.088 --> 00:48.173
Be quiet. Just come.

00:48.256 --> 00:49.924
Why were they all there?

00:50.008 --> 00:51.509
Did you call that scumbag, Si-woo?

00:53.094 --> 00:54.512
What's it to you?

00:54.596 --> 00:56.681
How dare you come here
at this hour and cause a scene?

00:56.765 --> 00:57.891
Why?

00:58.850 --> 01:00.894
Hey, Ha-kyung.

01:01.478 --> 01:03.063
Don't scare me like that.

01:03.146 --> 01:06.316
I'm scaring you? Is it okay
when you do it but scary when I do?

01:08.985 --> 01:11.029
Don't be so mean to me.

01:11.112 --> 01:14.157
I came here to apologize to you.

01:14.783 --> 01:16.284
What?

01:17.660 --> 01:19.913
I'm sorry, Ha-kyung.

01:23.708 --> 01:24.834
I'm sorry.

01:25.543 --> 01:26.753
I mean it.

01:27.378 --> 01:30.507
I'm truly sorry.

01:32.801 --> 01:35.887
I'm a real asshole.

01:41.100 --> 01:43.144
Didn't they call off their marriage?

01:44.062 --> 01:45.188
They did.

01:46.272 --> 01:47.649
Then why did he come here?

01:48.358 --> 01:49.484
I'm not sure.

01:52.195 --> 01:53.988
He seemed pretty wasted.

01:54.072 --> 01:55.448
Shouldn't we check on them?

01:57.408 --> 01:58.785
They'll take care of it.

02:01.746 --> 02:03.081
I'll go.

02:09.921 --> 02:11.214
I should get going too.

02:12.423 --> 02:13.591
Seok-ho.

02:15.927 --> 02:17.679
You live right upstairs?

02:17.762 --> 02:19.055
Yes. Why?

02:19.139 --> 02:20.223
I see.

02:22.392 --> 02:23.852
To be honest…

02:25.436 --> 02:27.272
I don't feel comfortable here.

02:27.355 --> 02:28.940
So I think--

02:29.023 --> 02:31.317
- You'll get used to it.
- Right?

02:31.401 --> 02:33.194
Of course. Rest up.

02:33.278 --> 02:34.696
Okay. Good night.

02:37.198 --> 02:39.033
What a rigid guy.

02:47.959 --> 02:50.503
Were you in this much pain too?

02:52.463 --> 02:54.090
What are you rambling about?

03:01.431 --> 03:04.392
When I betrayed you,

03:05.226 --> 03:06.728
did you also feel like

03:06.811 --> 03:10.773
your heart was being ripped into pieces?

03:11.441 --> 03:12.400
No.

03:12.483 --> 03:14.319
My heart tore into pieces

03:14.402 --> 03:17.530
because I was humiliated,
not because I was heartbroken.

03:18.448 --> 03:21.701
So please stop embarrassing me
and just go home. Okay?

03:25.330 --> 03:27.248
I see.

03:28.625 --> 03:31.711
My dear Ha-kyung was humiliated.

03:32.462 --> 03:35.632
So that was why you were in pain.

03:37.467 --> 03:39.135
Hey. Can you please…

03:39.677 --> 03:42.055
Are you crazy?
What's wrong with you today?

03:42.639 --> 03:43.723
Ha-kyung.

03:44.766 --> 03:47.310
I think I'm being punished.

03:47.393 --> 03:48.353
What?

03:49.479 --> 03:52.899
I'm being punished for betraying you.

03:58.196 --> 04:00.198
Hey, quit putting on a show.

04:00.281 --> 04:02.492
I'm still not going
to proofread your manuscript.

04:03.201 --> 04:04.577
Lee Si-woo…

04:06.913 --> 04:08.873
and Yu-jin

04:09.832 --> 04:13.127
had lived together
before she and I got married.

04:14.087 --> 04:16.422
What should I do, Ha-kyung?

04:17.674 --> 04:20.468
After all that I did to marry her?

04:22.637 --> 04:25.431
I gave you the worst heartbreak ever

04:25.515 --> 04:28.726
and became a terrible asshole.

04:30.019 --> 04:32.605
So how could she do this to me?

04:32.689 --> 04:38.611
How could she lie through her teeth?

04:41.322 --> 04:42.865
Let's get the facts straight.

04:44.075 --> 04:46.244
She didn't lie. She just didn't tell you.

04:47.120 --> 04:49.497
And you guys are already married.

04:49.580 --> 04:51.249
How would she feel

04:51.332 --> 04:53.960
to see you in pain
because of her undisclosed past?

04:55.712 --> 04:57.046
If you truly love someone,

04:57.714 --> 05:00.842
you should be able to embrace their past.

05:03.803 --> 05:05.263
Understood, Ki-jun?

05:07.598 --> 05:08.683
Are you sleeping?

05:09.517 --> 05:10.643
Hey.

05:12.520 --> 05:13.354
Hey.

05:14.480 --> 05:15.815
Are you crazy? Get off me.

05:15.898 --> 05:16.983
Wake up.

05:18.776 --> 05:19.861
Hey.

05:24.449 --> 05:25.616
Si-woo.

05:25.700 --> 05:27.493
Do you know where he lives?

05:29.620 --> 05:30.997
No, I don't.

05:56.606 --> 06:02.361
LEE SI-WOO

06:05.573 --> 06:07.283
LEE SI-WOO

06:08.451 --> 06:09.577
Yes?

06:10.161 --> 06:11.829
Why are you calling me at this hour?

06:30.598 --> 06:31.557
Ki-jun.

06:33.059 --> 06:34.519
I'm sorry.

06:35.353 --> 06:36.854
I am.

06:37.897 --> 06:39.065
What happened?

06:41.234 --> 06:42.902
Why are you dropping him off?

06:43.694 --> 06:45.571
Ask him if you're curious.

06:48.157 --> 06:49.242
Here.

06:58.292 --> 06:59.585
It's okay. Let me.

07:00.419 --> 07:02.505
Why did you drink so much?

07:03.506 --> 07:04.549
Ki-jun.

07:05.174 --> 07:07.218
Wake up, Ki-jun. Okay?

07:09.303 --> 07:10.847
Can you please wake up?

07:14.600 --> 07:16.769
Who did he drink this much with?

07:18.438 --> 07:19.814
I'm sorry.

07:20.773 --> 07:21.858
I am.

07:22.358 --> 07:23.734
Do you feel guilty?

07:25.194 --> 07:27.405
I'm truly sorry,

07:27.989 --> 07:29.365
Ha-kyung.

07:32.326 --> 07:33.661
I am

07:34.912 --> 07:38.499
really sorry, Ha-kyung.

08:29.467 --> 08:32.470
Mischievous weather
doesn't only pertain to cloudy skies,

08:33.221 --> 08:34.847
unexpected snow or rain,

08:35.765 --> 08:39.268
harsh winds, and typhoons.

08:45.358 --> 08:46.817
Why are you still out here?

08:48.486 --> 08:50.196
Did you drop him home?

08:51.447 --> 08:54.033
I'm sorry for making you do that.

08:54.825 --> 08:55.993
Let's go.

08:56.077 --> 08:57.870
Were you upset too?

08:58.454 --> 08:59.413
What do you mean?

09:00.206 --> 09:01.707
When I told you

09:02.291 --> 09:04.001
that I had lived with Yu-jin.

09:04.085 --> 09:06.504
Hot weather and high humidity

09:06.587 --> 09:08.881
strangely provoke you.

09:08.965 --> 09:10.883
Did you also feel betrayed

09:11.467 --> 09:13.094
like Ki-jun did?

09:17.348 --> 09:18.432
Well…

09:19.141 --> 09:20.977
I didn't feel betrayed.

09:22.186 --> 09:24.313
But I wasn't too happy
to hear about it either.

09:25.439 --> 09:27.066
Just like when I heard

09:27.650 --> 09:30.820
about how you had written
his columns for him?

09:30.903 --> 09:35.283
- You become cranky for no reason.
- Was it a similar feeling?

09:35.366 --> 09:36.867
How did you know about that?

09:39.120 --> 09:40.580
I just did.

09:40.663 --> 09:42.206
Then why didn't you tell me?

09:42.290 --> 09:43.541
Would it have changed anything?

09:43.624 --> 09:46.502
You pick a fight for no apparent reason.

09:46.586 --> 09:48.546
What is this?
Are you picking a fight with me?

09:48.629 --> 09:50.631
Then at least say something.

09:51.340 --> 09:54.594
We become victims of mischievous weather

09:55.928 --> 09:58.389
when we least expect it.

10:06.731 --> 10:07.940
Hey.

10:30.671 --> 10:32.465
Hey, you--

10:41.891 --> 10:44.352
Goodness, it's steaming hot in here.

10:45.478 --> 10:52.443
EPISODE 8
DISCOMFORT INDEX

11:45.538 --> 11:47.248
What happened last night?

11:50.042 --> 11:51.252
What do you mean?

11:52.002 --> 11:53.754
You were completely wasted,

11:53.838 --> 11:56.841
and Si-woo, of all people,
dropped you off.

11:56.924 --> 11:59.718
- Do you not remember?
- Let's talk about it later.

11:59.802 --> 12:02.721
No, explain it to me now.
I have to hear it right now.

12:05.641 --> 12:07.685
Let's just talk later, Yu-jin.

12:09.103 --> 12:12.064
What's wrong? Is something going on?

12:14.900 --> 12:16.193
I just need…

12:17.486 --> 12:19.405
some time to think.

12:20.030 --> 12:21.365
Bye.

12:36.172 --> 12:39.258
You should have just let them be.
I was going to clean up this morning.

12:39.341 --> 12:42.386
Please clean up after yourself
right away next time.

12:42.470 --> 12:44.513
It's not easy to get rid of the smell.

12:45.097 --> 12:46.724
Okay. I'll do that.

12:49.351 --> 12:50.728
Good morning…

12:51.312 --> 12:55.232
Microwavable food, top left shelf.
Plates and cutlery, top right shelf.

12:55.316 --> 12:57.902
Ingredients such as
bread, butter, jams, and milk

12:57.985 --> 13:00.279
are all inside the fridge.

13:00.362 --> 13:01.739
Help yourself to breakfast.

13:03.532 --> 13:04.575
See you later.

13:05.075 --> 13:06.285
Okay. Bye.

13:07.077 --> 13:09.038
We'll go to work soon.

13:16.003 --> 13:17.630
Do you want some ramyeon?

13:17.713 --> 13:19.173
- What?
- Where is it?

13:20.049 --> 13:22.176
The ramyeon is here.

13:23.886 --> 13:24.887
In here.

13:24.970 --> 13:27.848
And the pots

13:27.932 --> 13:30.434
- are over here.
- What?

13:32.269 --> 13:34.021
How did you know?

13:34.813 --> 13:35.940
Well…

13:36.023 --> 13:38.484
She just told us before she left.

13:39.068 --> 13:40.569
- Right.
- That's why.

13:42.071 --> 13:43.239
I'll boil the water.

13:43.322 --> 13:44.532
- Okay.
- Okay.

13:47.451 --> 13:50.162
Gosh. It's scorching hot this morning.

13:50.246 --> 13:52.122
- I'm going to shower first.
- Okay.

13:58.796 --> 14:03.300
Seoul will be hot this afternoon
with a temperature of over 30°C.

14:03.384 --> 14:04.635
It's quite humid as well.

14:04.718 --> 14:07.680
The discomfort index is 76.7.

14:07.763 --> 14:09.431
This is considered fairly high,

14:09.515 --> 14:12.518
and about half of the population
can easily get cranky.

14:13.102 --> 14:15.229
Although the temperature
hasn't changed much,

14:15.813 --> 14:17.773
the increase in humidity

14:17.856 --> 14:20.317
has made us more uncomfortable.

14:20.401 --> 14:22.736
The highest temperature is 31°C in Seoul

14:22.820 --> 14:24.071
and 30°C in Cheongju.

14:24.154 --> 14:25.823
Just like when I heard

14:26.407 --> 14:29.577
about how you had written
his columns for him?

14:30.160 --> 14:31.662
Was it a similar feeling?

14:45.926 --> 14:47.177
Why isn't it working?

14:59.189 --> 15:00.274
Damn it.

15:07.448 --> 15:08.449
Soo-jin.

15:08.949 --> 15:10.534
- Look at this.
- Hello.

15:10.618 --> 15:12.828
- Hello.
- Hello.

15:13.621 --> 15:15.372
- Hello.
- Hello.

15:15.915 --> 15:18.000
KOREA METEOROLOGICAL ADMINISTRATION

15:18.667 --> 15:19.960
Did you eat already?

15:20.753 --> 15:22.421
Make sure you eat before work.

15:22.504 --> 15:24.131
- Hello.
- Goodness.

15:35.768 --> 15:36.852
Thank you.

15:37.436 --> 15:39.188
Don't you feel hot?

15:39.939 --> 15:42.483
Not really. Maybe it's just a feeling.

15:43.233 --> 15:46.236
We had countless analyses
and discussions about this.

15:47.988 --> 15:50.032
The rainy season has finally started.

15:50.115 --> 15:51.492
You could just be tense.

15:51.575 --> 15:52.576
Maybe.

15:53.369 --> 15:54.578
Why is it suddenly so hot?

15:55.329 --> 15:56.372
I told you.

16:01.377 --> 16:03.045
Let me check.

16:06.465 --> 16:08.884
Hello, this is the Chief Team
of the Forecast Bureau.

16:08.968 --> 16:10.928
I think there's a problem
with the AC here.

16:11.595 --> 16:13.305
Really?

16:14.890 --> 16:16.433
But we're having a meeting soon.

16:17.351 --> 16:19.853
Okay. Please hurry.

16:22.314 --> 16:24.316
- Hello.
- Good morning.

16:25.859 --> 16:27.653
Why is it so hot in here?

16:27.736 --> 16:30.114
There's a problem
with the central cooling system.

16:30.197 --> 16:32.449
Maintenance is looking into it right now.

16:32.533 --> 16:35.327
Really? It just had to
break down on the hottest day.

16:35.411 --> 16:36.495
Right?

16:37.329 --> 16:39.039
Why isn't Director Jin here yet?

16:40.416 --> 16:41.583
I'm not sure.

16:42.459 --> 16:44.253
She left before we did.

16:54.513 --> 16:55.931
Hey, Ha-kyung. What is it?

16:56.015 --> 16:58.225
Isn't Areum Insurance
the insurance company for my car?

16:58.308 --> 17:01.979
Oh, that? I changed it
to Sang-hun's company six months ago.

17:02.062 --> 17:03.772
Without telling me?

17:08.485 --> 17:09.695
Excuse me.

17:09.778 --> 17:11.447
Call your insurance company.

17:11.530 --> 17:13.365
That's why I'm on the phone right now.

17:14.283 --> 17:16.076
Okay. What's the name of the company?

17:16.660 --> 17:18.954
- I'm in a hurry.
- I get it.

17:20.914 --> 17:22.499
Where are you? I'll go.

17:22.583 --> 17:23.500
Forget it.

17:23.584 --> 17:25.753
Just tell me the name
of the insurance company.

17:25.836 --> 17:29.006
I'll call them myself.
Just tell me where you are.

17:30.090 --> 17:34.136
The person you are trying to reach
is unavailable. Please try again…

17:38.098 --> 17:39.433
Okay.

17:39.516 --> 17:42.811
I hope everything works out. Okay, bye.

17:43.645 --> 17:45.105
- Sir.
- Yes?

17:45.189 --> 17:48.484
- Director Jin got into a car accident.
- What?

17:49.234 --> 17:50.569
Oh, dear.

17:51.487 --> 17:52.613
Is she hurt?

17:52.696 --> 17:54.490
No, she's not.

17:54.573 --> 17:56.450
I'll lead the meeting today.

17:56.533 --> 17:57.534
Okay.

17:59.912 --> 18:01.497
She got into an accident today

18:01.580 --> 18:03.582
when we had an important briefing?

18:03.665 --> 18:08.087
Gosh. Could this be an omen?

18:08.837 --> 18:10.422
Don't jinx it.

18:10.506 --> 18:12.925
Everyone's already on edge
due to the high discomfort index.

18:13.467 --> 18:15.302
Be careful what you say today, Ms. Kim.

18:15.385 --> 18:16.428
Yes, ma'am.

18:23.560 --> 18:25.604
Excuse me. Where is Spokesperson Han?

18:25.687 --> 18:29.358
Something urgent came up,
so he asked me to take over for him.

18:39.076 --> 18:41.370
We'll begin the meeting of June 27.

18:41.453 --> 18:42.871
Satellite Center?

18:43.455 --> 18:46.416
Judging by the satellite imagery
and the weather chart,

18:46.500 --> 18:50.295
there's a stationary front
on the very south side of Jeju Island.

18:51.004 --> 18:52.589
I heard you crashed your car.

18:53.173 --> 18:54.758
Call me when you read this.

18:59.930 --> 19:03.142
It'll be taken care of quickly
since no one was hurt.

19:03.225 --> 19:06.019
- Thank you.
- Please sign here.

19:10.023 --> 19:12.025
I'll call you later.

19:43.098 --> 19:45.225
I told you not to come,
so why are you here?

19:45.309 --> 19:47.227
I spoke with Sang-hun on my way here.

19:47.311 --> 19:50.355
He said he'll take care
of the collision coverage himself

19:50.439 --> 19:51.565
and call you afterward.

19:51.648 --> 19:54.193
Why did you change
the company without telling me?

19:54.276 --> 19:55.611
Do you know how flustered I was?

19:56.361 --> 19:57.654
I'm sorry.

19:57.738 --> 20:00.199
We had agreed to share the car
once we got married.

20:00.282 --> 20:02.701
The contract ended,
so I just helped out a friend.

20:03.368 --> 20:05.078
Who knew we'd break up?

20:05.162 --> 20:07.372
You're always like this.
You decide on your own,

20:07.456 --> 20:09.333
cause a mess, and I have to deal with it.

20:09.917 --> 20:11.376
That's why I'm here.

20:11.460 --> 20:13.503
I'm not glad to see you,
so don't do this again.

20:14.087 --> 20:15.881
Fine. Get in the car.
We're late for the meeting.

20:16.506 --> 20:17.466
I'm okay.

20:18.300 --> 20:20.677
Senior Forecaster Um
will lead the meeting.

20:20.761 --> 20:22.304
Since I'm late, I can just take a cab.

20:22.387 --> 20:23.388
What?

20:23.889 --> 20:26.391
Do you think a cab will
pick you up at an underpass?

20:30.687 --> 20:33.065
I HEARD YOU CRASHED YOUR CAR.
CALL ME WHEN YOU READ THIS.

20:34.358 --> 20:37.694
So you're saying that in five days,
the stationary front will cause rain

20:37.778 --> 20:41.281
to fall in Jeju
and the southern provinces?

20:41.365 --> 20:45.494
We should continue monitoring
the ocean's atmosphere.

20:45.577 --> 20:48.664
If the front suddenly switches directions
from north to south,

20:48.747 --> 20:50.374
there may be a delay.

20:50.457 --> 20:54.544
It'll be fine since the anticyclone
of the North Pacific is below it.

20:55.337 --> 20:59.007
If anything, it might rain
a day or two early.

20:59.091 --> 21:00.759
If you look at Jeju's sea,

21:00.842 --> 21:02.928
the atmosphere is barely moving.

21:03.637 --> 21:06.765
If the five-kilometer-high
pressure trough fails to support it

21:06.848 --> 21:09.017
- or if the anticyclone…
- What's going on?

21:09.601 --> 21:10.936
Are you hurt?

21:11.019 --> 21:13.563
Then the northward stationary front

21:13.647 --> 21:15.399
could suddenly go southward.

21:15.482 --> 21:18.443
If we were to measure it
at a five-kilometer distance,

21:18.527 --> 21:20.028
it will definitely happen.

21:21.363 --> 21:23.490
What's your take on this, Jeju Office?

21:23.573 --> 21:25.826
We agree with the Busan Office.

21:25.909 --> 21:27.411
Judging by the gale

21:27.494 --> 21:31.081
at the north of the stationary front
at a 200hPa altitude,

21:31.164 --> 21:33.083
it is definitely possible.

21:38.964 --> 21:41.591
NATIONAL METEOROLOGICAL CENTER
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

21:59.776 --> 22:01.528
If we forecast it a day or two later

22:01.611 --> 22:03.822
like Senior Forecaster Um said
and we're wrong,

22:03.905 --> 22:05.157
who'll take the blame?

22:05.240 --> 22:07.576
We'll receive even more public backlash

22:07.659 --> 22:09.786
if it starts raining earlier.

22:10.620 --> 22:12.039
Let's take a safer stance.

22:12.706 --> 22:15.000
No, I don't think that's right.

22:15.876 --> 22:20.088
The weather is being heavily affected
by climate change these days.

22:21.465 --> 22:24.843
In the past several years,
we continuously failed to forecast

22:24.926 --> 22:26.678
the end of the rainy season.

22:26.762 --> 22:29.181
Now, people don't believe in our forecast.

22:29.765 --> 22:33.185
If we fail to forecast
the start of the rainy season this year,

22:34.061 --> 22:36.980
we will receive
a ton of criticism this summer.

22:37.064 --> 22:38.982
So you want to risk it?

22:42.152 --> 22:44.946
Can we delay the press announcement?

22:47.824 --> 22:48.909
Is it possible?

22:48.992 --> 22:50.786
We've pushed it back as much as possible.

22:50.869 --> 22:53.330
After seeing
the southern stationary front,

22:53.413 --> 22:54.956
the press and local governments

22:55.040 --> 22:56.833
have been bombarding us with calls.

22:56.917 --> 23:00.670
If we're too late,
the press will write whatever they want.

23:00.754 --> 23:03.757
Don't you remember
what we had to go through last time?

23:03.840 --> 23:05.008
Forecaster Lee?

23:13.517 --> 23:14.559
Forecaster Lee Si-woo.

23:15.936 --> 23:16.978
What's your take?

23:27.614 --> 23:28.448
I'm sorry.

23:29.241 --> 23:30.867
I didn't follow.

23:30.951 --> 23:32.244
What were you doing?

23:33.286 --> 23:34.663
I'm sorry, sir.

23:37.541 --> 23:39.209
All right. What should we do?

23:40.210 --> 23:42.587
Due to central-northern China's trough

23:42.671 --> 23:44.548
and the formation of the gale,

23:44.631 --> 23:47.759
it's more likely that
the stationary front will head north.

23:48.385 --> 23:50.846
Should we say
the rainy season will start in five days?

23:52.764 --> 23:53.890
We have no choice.

23:53.974 --> 23:55.475
We can make that announcement.

23:57.018 --> 23:58.812
- Are you sure?
- Yes, sir.

24:02.899 --> 24:04.901
Okay. Good work, everyone.

24:04.985 --> 24:05.986
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

24:06.069 --> 24:09.197
Give a press briefing in the afternoon.

24:09.281 --> 24:11.199
Right. During the briefing,

24:11.283 --> 24:15.120
make sure you guys tell
the journalists that they shouldn't make

24:15.203 --> 24:17.622
a hasty conclusion
about the beginning and end dates

24:17.706 --> 24:18.999
- of the rainy season.
- Yes, sir.

24:19.082 --> 24:21.042
Okay. Good job working in the heat.

24:21.126 --> 24:23.795
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

24:43.607 --> 24:46.610
- What about the meeting?
- Assistant Director Kim took over for me.

24:47.402 --> 24:48.695
Good going.

24:53.116 --> 24:54.117
Sorry about yesterday.

24:55.076 --> 24:56.661
I was too drunk to control myself.

24:57.162 --> 24:58.788
Was I a terrible drunk?

25:00.749 --> 25:02.584
I'm sure you already know the answer.

25:04.211 --> 25:05.962
I'm sorry.

25:07.172 --> 25:09.382
- Go to the right lane.
- Okay.

25:10.425 --> 25:11.927
- The blinkers.
- Right.

25:19.142 --> 25:21.519
Habits are hard to break, right?

25:21.603 --> 25:22.771
Not really.

25:27.692 --> 25:30.237
Ha-kyung, what should I do?

25:31.613 --> 25:32.572
Divorce if you want.

25:32.656 --> 25:34.532
Don't make it sound so easy.

25:36.159 --> 25:37.369
I can't do that.

25:37.452 --> 25:39.204
I still love Yu-jin so much.

25:39.996 --> 25:41.248
Then stick with her.

25:41.831 --> 25:44.417
That bastard, Lee Si-woo, is to blame.

25:44.501 --> 25:45.543
Don't be absurd.

25:45.627 --> 25:46.878
This is between you and her.

25:47.504 --> 25:50.006
Why do you always
get worked up when I mention him?

25:51.216 --> 25:53.468
Because you always pick on him.

25:58.598 --> 26:00.267
Watch out, Ha-kyung.

26:00.892 --> 26:04.396
I could totally see that he's a womanizer.

26:07.607 --> 26:08.900
Focus on driving.

26:08.984 --> 26:10.151
Look at the road.

26:11.027 --> 26:13.738
And let me say this from
an older brother's point of view.

26:13.822 --> 26:15.573
Kick Senior Forecaster Um and that kid

26:15.657 --> 26:18.243
out of your house right now. Okay?

26:19.119 --> 26:20.537
Older brother, my ass.

26:21.204 --> 26:23.331
Whatever. They're my teammates.
I'll take care of it.

26:50.859 --> 26:52.277
Gosh, it's steaming hot.

26:55.363 --> 26:57.490
The computer center got their own AC,

26:57.574 --> 26:59.034
so it's freezing in there.

26:59.784 --> 27:01.202
So why is it so hot here?

27:01.286 --> 27:03.663
That's because they have many machines.

27:03.747 --> 27:06.791
I guess machines
are more important than humans.

27:07.500 --> 27:10.128
If that's true, shouldn't we receive
special treatment too?

27:10.211 --> 27:11.796
We also work like machines.

27:12.505 --> 27:13.590
I agree.

27:18.678 --> 27:20.138
Hello, sir.

27:29.898 --> 27:32.025
The feature story might fall through?

27:32.108 --> 27:33.818
What do you mean?

27:33.902 --> 27:38.740
Your husband suddenly
called us this morning

27:38.823 --> 27:41.242
and said he couldn't write it.

27:41.326 --> 27:43.703
He could have just said no
from the get-go!

27:43.787 --> 27:45.663
We've already finalized the format!

27:45.747 --> 27:46.873
How could he do this?

27:46.956 --> 27:49.459
Gosh. I'm sorry, sir.

27:50.377 --> 27:51.461
Gosh.

27:52.212 --> 27:54.756
I'll talk with him

27:55.465 --> 27:57.008
and call you back.

27:57.092 --> 27:58.426
I'm sorry, sir.

27:59.427 --> 28:00.595
Goodbye.

28:11.398 --> 28:14.275
Do you even know
how many computers we have here?

28:14.859 --> 28:17.487
We can't ventilate the room.
We're melting in here.

28:17.570 --> 28:20.657
I heard you provided
the computer center with an AC.

28:20.740 --> 28:22.534
Can you help us out too?

28:23.284 --> 28:24.160
When?

28:27.038 --> 28:29.416
Okay. Please hurry.

28:31.918 --> 28:33.086
What did they say?

28:33.169 --> 28:35.130
They can't get us a new one.

28:35.213 --> 28:37.257
They told us to wait another two hours.

28:37.340 --> 28:38.383
Again?

28:39.050 --> 28:41.177
They said that an hour ago.

28:44.597 --> 28:46.099
Can you talk to them in person?

28:47.183 --> 28:48.226
Me?

28:48.309 --> 28:50.103
You're good at persuading others.

28:55.775 --> 28:57.318
Hey, Forecaster…

29:01.281 --> 29:03.575
Forecaster Lee seems down all day.

29:04.534 --> 29:07.120
I bet it's because of the sweltering heat.

29:09.247 --> 29:10.790
What are you doing?

29:10.874 --> 29:12.167
Should I go instead?

29:12.250 --> 29:14.043
No.

29:14.127 --> 29:15.670
It's okay.

29:15.754 --> 29:17.380
I'll go.

29:19.174 --> 29:20.049
Thank you.

29:24.095 --> 29:26.097
AIR CONDITIONING ROOM
RESTRICTED ACCESS

29:30.560 --> 29:33.062
Excuse me, I'm from the Chief Team.

29:36.232 --> 29:38.234
Are they in there or not?

29:42.113 --> 29:44.073
When will you fix…

29:52.332 --> 29:53.958
How can I help you?

29:58.630 --> 30:00.715
Thank you for your hard work. Goodbye.

30:12.477 --> 30:13.686
Four.

30:14.312 --> 30:15.438
Four.

30:16.606 --> 30:18.817
One, two, three, four.

30:18.900 --> 30:21.611
Crocodiles' hind feet have four toes.

30:30.495 --> 30:31.621
Hey.

30:32.622 --> 30:35.792
They got Ha-kyung a blind date.

30:35.875 --> 30:37.752
The guy provided a few dates,

30:37.836 --> 30:40.296
so we can pick whichever one we want.

30:40.380 --> 30:42.590
Mom, are you still doing that?

30:42.674 --> 30:44.467
He's a gynecologist.

30:44.551 --> 30:48.304
He definitely has a promising future
and a high salary. Don't you think so?

30:48.888 --> 30:50.765
Can you please stop?

30:50.849 --> 30:53.059
She's busy due to
the disaster prevention season.

30:53.643 --> 30:56.646
And if you do this without her approval,

30:56.729 --> 30:58.439
she might never see you again.

31:00.024 --> 31:01.568
What if something happens to me

31:01.651 --> 31:04.904
like last time, and I pass away?

31:04.988 --> 31:08.116
Neither you nor Ha-kyung
will know what to do.

31:08.199 --> 31:12.328
Knowing that there is someone
who can hold my funeral

31:12.412 --> 31:14.414
will help me die in peace.

31:14.497 --> 31:15.415
Mother!

31:15.498 --> 31:16.749
You're not going to die!

31:16.833 --> 31:21.170
Then? Did you think
I'd take care of you two forever?

31:21.254 --> 31:22.630
I never said that.

31:22.714 --> 31:25.550
Then just shut it and help me out.

31:25.633 --> 31:26.885
Whatever!

31:26.968 --> 31:28.344
You guys can sort this out!

31:28.428 --> 31:29.596
Leave me out of this!

31:30.305 --> 31:32.432
You don't have to get involved.

31:32.515 --> 31:34.517
I already know what to do.

31:39.272 --> 31:42.025
I lost my train of thought
once again thanks to her.

31:43.067 --> 31:46.863
Gosh! I just can't focus!

32:12.639 --> 32:15.350
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

32:25.777 --> 32:27.820
What is it, Forecaster Lee?

32:30.573 --> 32:31.824
We need to talk.

32:33.368 --> 32:34.285
Okay.

32:42.752 --> 32:44.420
HONEY

32:52.387 --> 32:53.763
KI-JUN

33:03.773 --> 33:04.607
Hey…

33:12.573 --> 33:14.075
OFFICE OF SPOKESPERSON

33:26.671 --> 33:28.381
What is it? What's wrong?

33:30.508 --> 33:32.051
I heard you had an accident.

33:32.844 --> 33:33.970
Are you hurt?

33:35.680 --> 33:38.349
It was a minor collision.
They towed my car.

33:39.517 --> 33:41.519
Ki-jun could have suspected us back there.

33:41.602 --> 33:42.770
I wish he did.

33:43.396 --> 33:44.355
What?

33:44.439 --> 33:46.107
Why did you call

33:46.190 --> 33:48.317
Senior Forecaster Um first and not me?

33:48.901 --> 33:50.403
That was because of the meeting.

33:50.486 --> 33:53.781
Then why did you come back with Ki-jun?

33:55.158 --> 33:56.868
There was an insurance issue.

33:56.951 --> 33:59.412
Are there still things
that haven't been sorted out with him?

34:00.079 --> 34:01.289
What are they?

34:01.372 --> 34:02.790
How long will this last?

34:02.874 --> 34:05.334
Besides the columns,
the apologies, and the insurance,

34:06.335 --> 34:08.337
what else is left between you two?

34:12.050 --> 34:13.843
Why have you been like this
since yesterday?

34:13.926 --> 34:16.179
Because he's been pissing me off
since last night!

34:18.306 --> 34:19.432
Do you know

34:19.932 --> 34:21.893
how worried I was?

34:23.644 --> 34:26.230
You were in an accident,
but you weren't picking up.

34:26.981 --> 34:28.608
I couldn't ask anyone

34:28.691 --> 34:30.735
how badly injured you were.

34:31.319 --> 34:32.653
I had to hide my worries.

34:33.946 --> 34:37.450
I couldn't focus at all
during the meeting.

34:39.118 --> 34:41.287
I was worried sick about you.

34:45.458 --> 34:46.667
I found myself

34:47.335 --> 34:49.378
falling head over heels for her.

34:50.797 --> 34:54.300
But the deeper I fell, the more upset

34:55.009 --> 34:57.178
and mad I got.

35:00.139 --> 35:01.933
Since it was a minor accident

35:02.016 --> 35:03.601
and nobody got hurt,

35:03.684 --> 35:05.853
I didn't think you'd be this worried.

35:08.898 --> 35:10.149
I'm sorry.

35:13.027 --> 35:15.196
Stop saying that you're sorry.

35:15.279 --> 35:17.115
Whenever you apologize,

35:17.698 --> 35:19.367
I feel like a bad person.

35:35.174 --> 35:37.426
There is a briefing this afternoon
regarding the rainy season.

35:39.262 --> 35:40.471
You should get prepared.

36:08.374 --> 36:09.625
Wait.

36:14.839 --> 36:16.132
Can we talk?

36:19.927 --> 36:22.221
- From here, right?
- Right.

36:24.390 --> 36:25.683
I'm sorry I'm late.

36:25.766 --> 36:28.436
Hello. Is everything taken care of?

36:28.519 --> 36:30.313
Did you get hurt?

36:32.190 --> 36:34.650
- My car had some damage but I'm fine.
- I see.

36:34.734 --> 36:36.485
Are we having
a rainy season briefing later?

36:36.569 --> 36:39.697
- Yes.
- Can I see a summary of today's meeting?

36:39.780 --> 36:41.199
Let's see. Here.

36:41.949 --> 36:45.328
Nothing big has changed
since our meeting two days ago.

36:45.870 --> 36:49.749
There's a stationary front
over the sea near Okinawa.

36:49.832 --> 36:53.002
Due to the formation
of the trough and the gale

36:53.085 --> 36:54.629
in central-northern China,

36:54.712 --> 36:57.256
we believe the rainy season
will begin in five days,

36:57.340 --> 36:59.759
starting in Jeju
and the southern provinces.

37:01.010 --> 37:02.637
But there's a catch.

37:03.638 --> 37:04.555
What is it?

37:04.639 --> 37:07.975
The anticyclone over
the Okhotsk Sea is too great,

37:08.059 --> 37:10.269
and cold air from the north has come down.

37:10.353 --> 37:13.189
If the anticyclone
of the North Pacific weakens,

37:13.981 --> 37:15.733
it'll take longer

37:15.816 --> 37:17.777
for the stationary front to rise.

37:19.528 --> 37:21.155
And the numerical model?

37:21.239 --> 37:22.573
It's similar to yesterday's.

37:23.366 --> 37:24.450
What should we do?

37:25.326 --> 37:27.119
Forecaster Lee, what do you…

37:34.502 --> 37:35.544
Let's base the briefing

37:35.628 --> 37:37.672
on what we agreed on this morning.

37:37.755 --> 37:41.676
Your theory makes sense too,
but we have no immediate proof.

37:42.176 --> 37:44.303
All right. Let's do that.

37:44.387 --> 37:46.514
- Ms. Kim.
- Yes, ma'am.

37:46.597 --> 37:48.266
Get the forecast material
for the changes in China's trough.

37:48.349 --> 37:50.101
I'll be in the briefing room.

37:50.184 --> 37:51.018
Yes, ma'am.

38:03.322 --> 38:05.574
How did you meet my husband yesterday?

38:05.658 --> 38:08.703
We didn't meet. He just came.

38:09.287 --> 38:10.830
He visited you?

38:10.913 --> 38:12.164
No. Director Jin.

38:12.748 --> 38:14.542
He was wasted.

38:14.625 --> 38:17.378
Why? Why did he go there?

38:23.551 --> 38:24.969
Hurry up.

38:25.886 --> 38:27.430
I think your husband found out.

38:27.513 --> 38:28.806
About what?

38:28.889 --> 38:31.267
That you and I lived together.

38:34.145 --> 38:35.438
How?

38:35.521 --> 38:36.981
Did you tell him?

38:38.024 --> 38:39.317
Why would I?

38:39.400 --> 38:40.860
What would I get out of it?

38:45.990 --> 38:48.159
No wonder he was
acting strange this morning.

38:48.242 --> 38:49.785
What should I do?

38:50.453 --> 38:53.164
Come on. You didn't do anything wrong.

38:53.247 --> 38:55.875
Make sure he understands
that it was all in the past.

38:56.542 --> 38:58.002
Do you think it's that easy?

38:58.502 --> 39:00.921
Guys will never understand that.

39:01.005 --> 39:03.966
Even if it was in the past,
their imaginations will run wild.

39:04.050 --> 39:06.052
What should I do?

39:07.678 --> 39:10.931
We agreed to move in together
because we wanted to.

39:11.599 --> 39:14.393
And you told me
you weren't going to regret it.

39:15.227 --> 39:18.814
- Remember?
- I had a change of heart once we broke up.

39:19.607 --> 39:22.485
Back then, I really thought
I wasn't going to regret it.

39:23.110 --> 39:24.737
But I regret it so much now.

39:25.237 --> 39:26.447
Don't you?

39:27.031 --> 39:28.157
No.

39:28.240 --> 39:32.119
I don't regret anything
I put my heart into.

39:33.454 --> 39:34.914
Maybe for now.

39:34.997 --> 39:37.333
Once you fall in love with someone new,

39:37.416 --> 39:39.960
you won't be able to tell them the truth.

39:47.051 --> 39:48.928
I already told her.

39:52.223 --> 39:55.601
Si-woo, are you seeing someone right now?

39:55.684 --> 39:56.936
Yes.

39:57.520 --> 39:59.230
So be brave and tell him.

39:59.730 --> 40:01.565
If he truly loves you,

40:01.649 --> 40:03.984
he should love the person you were

40:04.068 --> 40:05.736
in the past as well.

40:25.423 --> 40:26.674
Forecaster Lee.

40:26.757 --> 40:28.008
Yes, sir.

40:28.092 --> 40:29.260
Where have you been?

40:30.719 --> 40:31.971
What's with you today?

40:32.054 --> 40:33.889
You couldn't focus during the meeting.

40:33.973 --> 40:35.808
Don't work halfheartedly.

40:36.392 --> 40:37.685
I'm sorry, sir.

40:38.269 --> 40:39.979
It's because of the heat.

40:40.062 --> 40:41.730
No one can stand this heat.

40:44.942 --> 40:46.444
Ms. Kim, can you give me that?

40:47.611 --> 40:49.989
This is the forecast material
for the trough changes.

40:50.072 --> 40:52.366
Take this to the briefing room.

40:52.450 --> 40:54.743
Come to your senses and get up to date.

40:56.996 --> 40:57.997
Yes, sir.

41:04.753 --> 41:05.838
Could he be sick?

41:11.552 --> 41:13.679
Gosh, it's too hot today.

41:29.737 --> 41:31.447
Do I know her?

41:33.407 --> 41:34.992
Your girlfriend.

41:35.075 --> 41:37.870
You're not dating a colleague, are you?

41:45.669 --> 41:48.881
That's roughly all the information
about the start of the rainy season.

41:48.964 --> 41:52.676
Director Jin from Chief Team Two
will answer further questions.

41:59.475 --> 42:01.435
Hello, I'm Director Jin
from Chief Team Two.

42:01.519 --> 42:02.978
Any questions?

42:06.148 --> 42:08.025
I'm Reporter Cho Eun-ji from JBC.

42:08.108 --> 42:10.069
We were informed that
the seasonal rain front

42:10.152 --> 42:12.446
would last longer than usual this year.

42:12.530 --> 42:13.614
Why is this?

42:13.697 --> 42:16.408
That's because we predict
North Pacific's anticyclone

42:16.492 --> 42:18.160
would reach China and stay there.

42:18.827 --> 42:21.247
Then when will this rainy season end?

42:21.330 --> 42:23.999
We expect it to last
two to three days more.

42:24.083 --> 42:26.585
I'd like to clarify some terms for you.

42:41.600 --> 42:43.936
It's difficult to predict when it will end

42:44.019 --> 42:45.604
because we've been experiencing

42:45.688 --> 42:49.400
unusual weather during the summer
due to climate change.

42:49.483 --> 42:50.818
So instead of giving you

42:50.901 --> 42:53.654
the exact start and end dates
of the rainy season,

42:53.737 --> 42:57.116
we'll give short-range
and weekly forecasts regarding the rain.

43:01.078 --> 43:02.121
Director Jin, here.

43:05.624 --> 43:07.209
Next question, please.

43:09.628 --> 43:12.715
I saw you two coming in together.
What's going on?

43:12.798 --> 43:15.467
Never mind.

43:17.261 --> 43:19.638
"Never mind"? What do you mean?

43:19.722 --> 43:22.182
I'm not the type who minds about the past.

43:22.766 --> 43:23.934
What did you say?

43:24.518 --> 43:26.270
I'm also not the type to torment my lover

43:26.353 --> 43:28.647
with the past she had before dating me.

43:28.731 --> 43:30.524
And I'm definitely not a pathetic loser

43:30.608 --> 43:32.651
who barges into his ex-girlfriend's house.

43:52.546 --> 43:55.591
Rumor has it that
she lived with someone from the KMA.

43:55.674 --> 43:58.969
Did she end up marrying that guy?

43:59.053 --> 44:03.307
She lived with someone from the KMA?

44:03.390 --> 44:06.143
- How could she do that?
- She lived with someone from the KMA?

44:06.226 --> 44:08.312
She lived with someone?

45:05.077 --> 45:06.203
This is all your fault!

45:06.286 --> 45:07.663
Can't you see?

45:07.746 --> 45:08.789
What is he doing?

45:11.250 --> 45:12.668
Just be honest.

45:12.751 --> 45:15.170
Don't pretend to be
a gentleman and torment her.

45:15.254 --> 45:16.672
Be a man, will you?

45:16.755 --> 45:17.798
What did you say?

45:19.675 --> 45:20.509
Hey.

45:21.885 --> 45:23.387
- Stop fighting!
- Hey.

45:23.470 --> 45:24.596
- What did you say?
- Ki-jun!

45:24.680 --> 45:25.681
- Ki-jun!
- Damn it!

45:26.348 --> 45:27.641
Stop it, Lee Si-woo!

45:27.724 --> 45:29.268
- Come on!
- Stop them!

45:32.187 --> 45:33.981
- Stop it!
- Come on!

45:34.064 --> 45:35.399
Stop filming.

45:35.482 --> 45:37.025
What the hell did you say?

45:37.109 --> 45:38.610
Hey! You want a piece of me?

45:38.694 --> 45:39.820
You…

45:39.903 --> 45:41.780
- Record this. Hurry.
- You…

45:41.864 --> 45:43.157
- Don't film.
- Let go!

45:43.240 --> 45:45.742
Let me go! I said let go!

45:47.578 --> 45:49.329
I'm going to kill you today!

45:49.413 --> 45:51.331
- You little…
- Come here!

45:51.415 --> 45:52.499
Let me go!

45:52.583 --> 45:55.377
You're dead meat! You!

45:55.461 --> 45:57.045
FORECAST BUREAU DIRECTOR GENERAL
KO BONG-CHAN

45:57.880 --> 45:59.506
Good going.

46:06.138 --> 46:07.639
Okay? Well done.

46:10.934 --> 46:12.895
This is unbelievable.

46:14.104 --> 46:17.566
I thought you were just a couple of nerds,
but you knew how to fight.

46:17.649 --> 46:19.735
So tell me. Why did you fight?

46:19.818 --> 46:23.155
Are you not going to tell me
why you beat up each other?

46:28.118 --> 46:29.203
No?

46:32.706 --> 46:33.749
Fine.

46:34.583 --> 46:35.584
Assistant Director Park.

46:36.168 --> 46:37.044
Yes, sir?

46:37.127 --> 46:38.462
Get their written apologies

46:39.296 --> 46:41.006
and take disciplinary action.

46:41.507 --> 46:42.549
Yes, sir.

46:47.513 --> 46:49.389
My goodness.

47:04.655 --> 47:06.532
What in the world is going on?

47:06.615 --> 47:09.701
It's just too hot today.
Even the AC is broken.

47:10.327 --> 47:11.912
That's still no reason to fight.

47:13.747 --> 47:15.415
In front of the reporters at that.

47:19.503 --> 47:21.088
Breaking news!

47:22.047 --> 47:23.590
Deputy Director Han's wife.

47:23.674 --> 47:24.675
Reporter Chae Yu-jin?

47:24.758 --> 47:28.011
Who do you think her ex-boyfriend was?

47:29.471 --> 47:31.098
No way. It can't be.

47:31.181 --> 47:32.224
That's right.

47:32.307 --> 47:35.018
- It was Forecaster Lee.
- What?

47:39.648 --> 47:40.774
Seriously?

47:41.608 --> 47:43.110
Then what is this?

47:43.694 --> 47:45.362
Are you saying

47:45.445 --> 47:49.032
her husband and her ex-boyfriend
had a fight over her?

47:50.284 --> 47:52.578
But why? She's married.

47:53.161 --> 47:54.997
Maybe she's still seeing Forecaster Lee.

47:56.206 --> 47:57.291
I doubt it.

47:57.916 --> 48:00.794
Si-woo is not the type who's indecisive.

48:01.378 --> 48:03.088
He's not the type

48:03.171 --> 48:04.756
to cling on to his ex-girlfriend.

48:05.591 --> 48:08.635
I'm sure something else upset him.

48:08.719 --> 48:11.513
- So what could it be?
- Exactly. What could it be?

48:12.097 --> 48:13.223
I don't know the details.

48:14.224 --> 48:16.476
But if anything,
Ki-jun probably did him wrong.

48:17.394 --> 48:19.646
I know Ki-jun quite well.

48:20.647 --> 48:21.773
And he's a loser.

48:25.110 --> 48:28.405
So how about we just turn
a blind eye to today's incident?

48:28.488 --> 48:31.825
I'm sure it was a tough day
for Forecaster Lee as well.

48:33.535 --> 48:34.620
You're right.

48:34.703 --> 48:37.789
It's no fun to gossip
about someone's past.

48:38.624 --> 48:41.585
I completely agree with you.

48:42.336 --> 48:43.170
Me too.

48:49.092 --> 48:50.218
Sure.

49:04.900 --> 49:06.818
Hey, the AC is back on.

49:09.988 --> 49:11.740
You fixed this for us by going down there.

49:12.908 --> 49:15.702
Well, I didn't fix anything.

49:19.081 --> 49:20.082
It must be so hot.

49:21.458 --> 49:22.668
Thank you.

49:22.751 --> 49:24.127
- Thank you.
- My pleasure.

49:24.211 --> 49:25.504
And…

49:25.587 --> 49:27.047
Gosh.

49:28.215 --> 49:30.425
- Have some before you continue.
- Thank you.

49:30.509 --> 49:31.760
Thank you.

49:32.260 --> 49:33.303
Thank you.

49:34.054 --> 49:35.472
Gosh, that's nice.

49:35.555 --> 49:36.973
It's so refreshing.

49:48.402 --> 49:50.278
Oh, dear.

49:50.362 --> 49:52.072
UPCOMING RAINY SEASON
WILL BE HOT AND WORSE

49:52.155 --> 49:53.949
LOCAL GOVERNMENTS PREPARE
FOR THE RAINY SEASON

50:39.703 --> 50:40.954
What's going on?

50:45.917 --> 50:48.378
Ma'am, I'll be going now.

50:48.462 --> 50:49.671
Ms. Lee.

50:49.755 --> 50:50.964
Here.

50:53.008 --> 50:55.719
You could have just wired
the tutor fee as usual.

50:55.802 --> 50:58.346
I've already wired the tutor fee.

50:58.430 --> 51:00.223
This is just a small gift.

51:01.975 --> 51:03.226
Thank you.

51:04.936 --> 51:08.565
By the way, are you having
family problems these days?

51:09.399 --> 51:11.318
No. Why do you ask?

51:11.401 --> 51:16.198
My kid tells me that you have trouble
focusing during your lessons.

51:17.491 --> 51:18.366
Goodness.

51:18.450 --> 51:21.203
You know that kids these days
are more aware now, right?

51:21.286 --> 51:23.163
I trust that you'll do well.

51:23.955 --> 51:26.374
Okay. I'll be more careful.

51:27.501 --> 51:28.877
Goodbye.

51:28.960 --> 51:30.712
Goodbye. Thank you.

52:15.549 --> 52:19.386
CALLS

52:19.469 --> 52:22.222
BO-MI'S DAD

52:33.692 --> 52:36.111
KMA ANNOUNCES
THIS YEAR'S RAINY SEASON PROSPECT

52:48.915 --> 52:50.500
WIFE

52:53.837 --> 52:56.298
- Hello?
- Where are you?

52:57.632 --> 52:59.718
I'm at work of course.

52:59.801 --> 53:00.927
Where exactly?

53:01.928 --> 53:03.305
In the night-duty room.

53:04.180 --> 53:05.557
Aren't you uncomfortable?

53:06.182 --> 53:07.100
Well…

53:07.684 --> 53:10.061
I'm too busy to even feel uncomfortable.

53:10.729 --> 53:13.690
We had to announce the rainy season,
so it's been hectic all day.

53:13.773 --> 53:15.525
I'm finally resting now.

53:16.359 --> 53:17.652
You must be tired.

53:18.403 --> 53:20.030
I'm okay.

53:21.615 --> 53:22.699
Yes.

53:24.743 --> 53:26.202
Okay. Bye.

53:26.786 --> 53:28.538
How is Bo-mi…

53:49.976 --> 53:51.227
What did he say?

53:51.311 --> 53:53.355
He's already at home, right?

53:53.980 --> 53:55.398
Yes.

53:55.482 --> 53:57.359
I told you he left earlier.

53:59.527 --> 54:01.613
I should get going then.

54:01.696 --> 54:03.031
Goodbye.

54:03.865 --> 54:05.575
Goodbye. Have a safe way home.

54:31.643 --> 54:32.894
Goodness.

54:40.819 --> 54:41.903
Bear with it.

54:54.332 --> 54:55.417
Okay.

54:57.711 --> 55:00.088
Gosh, were you always a baby?

55:01.089 --> 55:03.133
So what? Do you not like me?

55:03.675 --> 55:05.260
How did you manage to fight?

55:05.343 --> 55:08.096
He threw a punch first.

55:08.179 --> 55:09.723
Should I have done nothing then?

55:11.975 --> 55:13.184
Stop being angry.

55:15.812 --> 55:18.106
Both the columns
and the insurance were my fault.

55:18.189 --> 55:20.400
This may sound odd.

55:20.483 --> 55:23.778
But since he and I
have known each other for ten long years,

55:24.362 --> 55:27.157
there are things
that I just can't easily cut off.

55:29.534 --> 55:31.453
For example, the morning incident.

55:32.037 --> 55:35.915
He didn't even tell me
that he had bought his friend's insurance.

55:35.999 --> 55:37.959
Imagine how flustered I was.

55:38.043 --> 55:40.670
The other driver demanded
that I call my insurance company.

55:42.756 --> 55:46.009
The reason why
I didn't explain this to you

55:46.634 --> 55:49.387
was because I didn't want you to know

55:50.180 --> 55:52.223
how pathetic my past relationship was.

55:52.849 --> 55:54.059
That's why.

55:55.060 --> 55:56.227
If that's the case,

55:57.395 --> 55:58.646
why are you telling me now?

56:00.899 --> 56:03.234
Being embarrassed
in front of you is temporary.

56:03.860 --> 56:05.653
But I'd regret it forever

56:06.529 --> 56:08.948
if you misunderstood me.

56:13.912 --> 56:16.498
I'll make sure
this doesn't happen ever again.

56:17.791 --> 56:23.713
Of course, bits of my past with Ki-jun
might suddenly surface out of nowhere.

56:25.590 --> 56:28.635
But I promise I'll be honest with you.

56:29.594 --> 56:30.929
I won't hide anything.

56:31.513 --> 56:32.430
You have my word.

56:39.104 --> 56:40.814
This is getting out of hand.

56:42.357 --> 56:43.942
Why? Are you still mad?

56:45.985 --> 56:49.197
I keep falling for you.

56:50.615 --> 56:52.325
It's getting out of hand.

56:57.247 --> 57:00.917
What if I love you so much
that I want others to know?

57:02.127 --> 57:05.463
That would be terrible
since our relationship would be over.

57:13.263 --> 57:15.098
We're in a public place.

57:15.682 --> 57:17.225
But it's not our office.

57:17.308 --> 57:19.018
What if someone we know sees us?

57:20.687 --> 57:22.313
If you're so worried about that,

57:22.397 --> 57:25.984
you shouldn't have sat next to me
with that beautiful smile,

57:26.067 --> 57:27.193
Ha-kyung.

57:29.571 --> 57:31.281
"Ha-kyung"? Did you just--

57:33.158 --> 57:34.242
What's wrong with you?

58:00.143 --> 58:01.394
No way.

58:17.035 --> 58:18.203
What are you doing there?

58:21.247 --> 58:22.624
You have something to say.

58:23.708 --> 58:24.876
Don't you?

58:28.379 --> 58:30.507
I'm tired. Maybe next time.

58:31.591 --> 58:33.426
Yes, we did live together.

58:35.512 --> 58:38.348
Si-woo and I lived together for a while.

58:38.932 --> 58:40.099
So what?

58:40.642 --> 58:44.020
It was before I met you,
so why is it so bad?

58:44.103 --> 58:45.980
Living with your boyfriend isn't a sin.

58:47.482 --> 58:48.650
Living together?

58:57.492 --> 58:59.077
Of course, it's not a sin.

58:59.160 --> 59:02.163
I know it's neither immoral nor illegal.

59:02.247 --> 59:03.456
I know that very well.

59:03.998 --> 59:06.084
But I'm in so much pain, Yu-jin.

59:07.919 --> 59:10.171
"Let's forget I heard it. Ignore it."

59:10.255 --> 59:12.090
I keep telling myself that.

59:13.424 --> 59:15.760
But I can't stop thinking about it.

59:17.804 --> 59:20.515
I can't accept the fact that you lived

59:22.141 --> 59:24.143
with another man, Yu-jin.

59:24.978 --> 59:27.897
And I despise that it was Lee Si-woo.

59:29.148 --> 59:31.276
It was before you and I dated.

59:31.359 --> 59:32.902
It's all in the past.

59:32.986 --> 59:35.113
Who said it's only in the past?

59:35.196 --> 59:37.490
What are you saying? I've moved on.

59:37.574 --> 59:38.908
Do you know…

59:41.911 --> 59:43.079
Damn it.

59:45.498 --> 59:48.376
Do you know who he's dating right now?

59:50.044 --> 59:53.256
Mischievous weather
doesn't only pertain to cloudy skies,

59:53.840 --> 59:55.675
unexpected snow or rain,

59:56.217 --> 59:59.554
harsh winds, and typhoons.

01:00:00.179 --> 01:00:02.265
Who is he dating?

01:00:05.852 --> 01:00:07.061
Jin Ha-kyung.

01:00:12.108 --> 01:00:13.318
What?

01:00:14.110 --> 01:00:15.111
Who?

01:00:15.194 --> 01:00:16.654
My ex-girlfriend.

01:00:17.280 --> 01:00:19.449
My ex-fiancée, Jin Ha-kyung.

01:00:20.033 --> 01:00:21.784
Director Jin from Chief Team Two!

01:00:31.794 --> 01:00:34.047
We become victims of mischievous weather

01:00:35.298 --> 01:00:38.009
when we least expect it.

01:00:49.646 --> 01:00:51.230
At times like these,

01:00:51.314 --> 01:00:54.359
a rain shower
would be wonderful and refreshing.

01:01:10.083 --> 01:01:12.585
There's no rain. I knew it.

01:01:16.422 --> 01:01:19.509
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

01:01:52.500 --> 01:01:54.544
- Are you dating Lee Si-woo?
- What?

01:01:54.627 --> 01:01:57.088
Aren't you just jealous
because they're going out?

01:01:57.171 --> 01:01:59.006
Jealous? Of Si-woo?

01:01:59.090 --> 01:02:00.717
Why don't we just come out?

01:02:00.800 --> 01:02:02.009
We have to play innocent.

01:02:03.219 --> 01:02:07.098
I'm sure Si-woo approached Ha-kyung
to get back at me.

01:02:07.682 --> 01:02:09.183
How is it coming along?

01:02:09.976 --> 01:02:11.644
Isn't making hasty conclusions
your specialty?

01:02:12.603 --> 01:02:14.689
Why don't you two have a debate about it?

01:02:15.857 --> 01:02:16.983
You should stop seeing her.

01:02:17.567 --> 01:02:19.068
Ha-kyung doesn't sincerely date anyone

01:02:20.319 --> 01:02:21.529
if they're not a marriage prospect.

01:02:22.196 --> 01:02:27.076
Subtitle translation by: Soo-ji Kim
